abstract:
We consider an obstacle problem in the Heisenberg group framework, and we prove that the operator on the obstacle bounds pointwise the operator on the solution. More explicitly, if $ε\ge0$ and $ ar u_ε$ minimizes the functional $$ \int_Ω(ε+|
abla_{\H^n}u|^2)^{p/2}$$ among the functions with prescribed Dirichlet boundary condition that stay below a smooth obstacle $ψ$, then 0 \le ÷_{\H^n}\, \Big((ε+|
abla_{\H^n} ar u_ε|^2)^{(p/2)-1} 
abla_{\H^n} ar u_ε\Big) \qquad \le (÷_{\H^n}\, \Big((ε+|
abla_{\H^n}ψ|^2)^{(p/2)-1} 
abla_{\H^n}ψ\Big))^+.
